{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/992033-so-i-finally-got-the-m20-core-book-my-complaints-aren-t-what-i-expected-them-to-be","id":992033,"title":"So I finally got the M20 core book.. My complaints aren't what I expected them to be.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-23T14:56:06-07:00","id":992033,"title":"So I finally got the M20 core book.. My complaints aren't what I expected them to be.","content":"So, thanks to the only local game turning to M20.... I had to make the plunge. Kinda annoyed me but.<br /> <br /> Now that I've had a look at it, I expected certain things to annoy me, and to a certain degree they do. The technephandi seem MASSIVELY overplayed here on these boards given it's essentially a disparate tinfoil hat theory.<br /> <br /> What annoys me instead are the Disparate Alliance, and the codified paradigms and practices.<br /> <br /> Firstly, I feel like the Disparate Alliance gutted a number of the independent crafts and combined them into a hamfisted alliance billed on equal parts paranoid conspiracy theory and &quot;We're not white! The western devils are to blame for EVERYTHING.&quot;<br /> <br /> Secondly, And I feel this is largely connected to the first. The one size fits all Paradigm descriptions, while they speed play and character creation, distract from the internal philosophy of each faction and reduce them to interchangeable buzzwords. THIS is why the Disparate alliance felt so.... empty. Because all the intricate beliefs about how and why they do what they do were replaced with politics. Everything was about how the other two factions screwed them over and so they needed to make a third.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T15:03:52-07:00","id":992040,"title":"","content":"The Technocracy-Nephandi thing is covered in more places than Mage 20.<br /> <br /> Also, there's plenty of white people among the Disparates (Knights Templar, for example). Yes, many of the Disparate groups are bitter about colonialism and imperialism (and rightfully so) but that's not really the major defining factor for the alliance. The fact that the Technocracy tried to wipe the Disparates out in the late 90s is pretty relevant, as is the fact that the Traditions didn't exactly rush to help them.<br /> <br /> As far as the paradigm descriptions, it's about time they offered some guidance. No one is restricted to these, as they're all examples. They just cover so much territory that most people won't have to look outside the provided lists.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T15:17:09-07:00","id":992051,"title":"","content":"I never said there wasn't. The Children of knowledge and Hollow Ones are non-racial as well. That was never my complaint. My complaint was that there's STILL a strong &quot;We're those non-European guys and EVERYTHING is the Europeans fault.&quot; The Kopa Loa have that vibe, the Ngoma have it, the Bata'a have it. The Wu Lung sort of have it. And everyone else just kind of.... ignores that. There's no real mention of internal friction beyond the Hypolotoi and the Knights Templar having their single sex recruitment thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T15:20:12-07:00","id":992055,"title":"","content":"Well, the Kopa Loa have very damned good reasons for holding such a perspective, and approaching them in an ahistorical fashion does neither them nor the setting any favors. The same applies to the other Disparates with a similar outlook.<br /> <br /> Don't get defensive about their views, try to do some research and understand it. They're based on real world grievances, after all.<br /> <br /> The historical <i>in-game</i> reasons seem to be covered adequately in Mage 20. For example, how the Traditions formed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T15:29:26-07:00","id":992062,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/992033-so-i-finally-got-the-m20-core-book-my-complaints-aren-t-what-i-expected-them-to-be?p=992051#post992051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I never said there wasn't. The Children of knowledge and Hollow Ones are non-racial as well. That was never my complaint. My complaint was that there's STILL a strong &quot;We're those non-European guys and EVERYTHING is the Europeans fault.&quot; The Kopa Loa have that vibe, the Ngoma have it, the Bata'a have it. The Wu Lung sort of have it. And everyone else just kind of.... ignores that. There's no real mention of internal friction beyond the Hypolotoi and the Knights Templar having their single sex recruitment thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>All of those sound like groups who were screwed over by Europe pretty recently - in living memory for some mages, I'd imagine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>We don't allow mages to cast spells, since this is the most unbalancing rule of all.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5226-jachra","name":"Jachra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T15:40:29-07:00","id":992073,"title":"","content":"See, here's the thing. I wouldn't have a problem with them, and in fact I rather like the Ngoma and Wu Lung. But it pisses me off that that and &quot;THE NEPHANDI ARE EVERYWHERE.&quot; are the only defining traits of the Disparates. There's no group ideology. No nothing. Just.... grievances with the other two and paranoid conspiracies.<br /> <br /> The others have their mystical mission statements. The Technocracy wants a one world order. One set of rules for all. The Traditions want a multitude of rules and styles.<br /> <br /> What do the Disparates want aside from to punch those other two in the face? What binds them together? The Ali Bahtin are cited as one of the founding members but they only joined because the Technocracy is supposedly controlled by the Nephandi. According to who? According to, at the time the Children of Knowledge. Because the organization of subtle scholars who observe people for years just happen to be hanging out in &quot;the global club scene.&quot; alongside the LSD tripping rave cultists.<br /> <br /> The Sisters of Hypolita make the LEAST sense out of all because the Technocracy is explicitly not a patriarchy and seeks to eliminate any form of gender, or racial discrimination. So the random appeal to real-world politics makes even LESS sense. The other have ostensibly true grievances with their real world tie ins. The Technocracy is hardly big on preserving native cultures. And is in fact downright HOSTILE to such.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T15:49:41-07:00","id":992076,"title":"","content":"It's not a random appeal to real-world politics. These disparates are based on real world cultures, and the politics relevant to those cultures are relevant to the disparates derived from those cultures.<br /> <br /> The Technocracy is part of the power, which means it partakes heavily of patriarchy and racial discrimination. In fact, I don't recall reading anywhere that the Technocracy is opposed to racism or sexism, so you're going to need to cite that.<br /> <br /> Regarding the Sisters of Hippolyta, they're also one of the Disparate crafts whom the Technocracy did their level best to violently expunge from the world in the late 90s. They have plenty of reasons to hate the Technocracy.<br /> <br /> The fact that the Technocracy is hostile to preserving indigenous cultures is a very big reason for those Disparate crafts to dislike - even <i>hate</i> - them. What with several of them being based on indigenous cultures.<br /> <br /> Also, don't whitewash the Technocracy. While individuals within the Union can be decent people, the organization as a whole represents much of what is wrong with western civilization. They've been a fascist organization since their introduction, and continue to be such in Mage 20.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T16:11:49-07:00","id":992086,"title":"","content":"I was under the impression that Wu Lung were not all that interested in the Traditions outside of the Akashics, and where more about trying to regain their seats of power in China from the Five Metal Dragons who run everything in the east these days.<br /> <br /> I will say, however, that the picture they chose for the Sisters of Hyppolyta isn't exactly flattering. But that's more an aesthetic thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T16:16:53-07:00","id":992090,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Guide to the Technocracy</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Bigot (2 pt Flaw)</b><br /> You just can\u2019t stand \u201cthose people,\u201d whoever \u201cthey\u201d might be. Maybe you\u2019re an Adamite who disdains the constructs, LERMUs, cyborgs and HIT Marks that you\u2019re forced to deal with. Or perhaps you\u2019re one of those superior life forms, sick and tired of taking up slack for your obsolete human colleagues. <b>Or you just can\u2019t deal with the Technocracy\u2019s ideal of equality, and you want to see those damn (blacks, gays, women, fill in the blank) put back in their proper place</b>. Either way, you\u2019ve got problems with your associates. You don\u2019t like them, and they probably don\u2019t like you. Whoever you hate, you have to learn to deal with them. <b>Open prejudice is liable to get you in trouble \u2014 bigotry is counterproductive, and the Union has no room for it.</b> Still, it just bugs you. Whenever you can, stay among Your Own Kind, and show those other assholes who\u2019s boss\u2026 without getting caught.</div> </div> </div> </div>Important parts bolded.<br /> <br /> Ok. That doesn't explain why they didn't sign on. The given explanation is they're fighting the &quot;Technocratic Patriarchy&quot; and that's what caused the Technocracy's ire. So either they're idiots or there must be something more. This is again, a problem of the one size fits all paradigm. Because it gives the &quot;Radical Feminist&quot; thing the front line rather than the Sisters specific BELIEFS that actually bring them out of line with the Technocracy. Which causes weird confusion.<br /> <br /> And I said I got that and didn't mind that. I just wished there was something more than what amounts to a bunch of fiercely independent nationalists banding together. Why did the Taftani join? Why did the Taftani abandon their &quot;Paradox is the mark of courage. The Traditions are cowards for acting coincidentally.&quot; hardliner attitude when they were actually WINNING in the middle east?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T16:54:29-07:00","id":992107,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/992033-so-i-finally-got-the-m20-core-book-my-complaints-aren-t-what-i-expected-them-to-be?p=992090#post992090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Important parts bolded.<br /> <br /> Ok. That doesn't explain why they didn't sign on. The given explanation is they're fighting the &quot;Technocratic Patriarchy&quot; and that's what caused the Technocracy's ire. So either they're idiots or there must be something more. This is again, a problem of the one size fits all paradigm. Because it gives the &quot;Radical Feminist&quot; thing the front line rather than the Sisters specific BELIEFS that actually bring them out of line with the Technocracy. Which causes weird confusion.<br /> <br /> And I said I got that and didn't mind that. I just wished there was something more than what amounts to a bunch of fiercely independent nationalists banding together. Why did the Taftani join? Why did the Taftani abandon their &quot;Paradox is the mark of courage. The Traditions are cowards for acting coincidentally.&quot; hardliner attitude when they were actually WINNING in the middle east?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's worth noting that some of the Convention Books touch on a very real problem the Technocracy has with misogyny in its ranks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T17:46:16-07:00","id":992126,"title":"","content":"It's also worth noting that despite the best of intentions, racism, sexism, homophobia, transphobia, etc. still exist in environments where at least lip service is given to the idea of not allowing them. That the Technocracy has overt policy regarding these things is not a sign of enlightened (ahem) perspectives, but more likely a sign that they do exist within the ranks and leadership and getting rid of them is an ideal, and not necessarily one everyone has bought into.<br /> <br /> The bigot flaw you quote describes the overt, obvious type of bigot, the kind of person who often serves as a stand-in to prove that someone isn't really racist, sexist, etc. &quot;It's not like I'm a member of the KKK&quot; etc. Even though people hold a lot of racist, sexist, homophobic, transphobic, and ableist attitudes without loudly proclaiming them from the rooftops, and you're more likely to encounter that then the overt bigoted hatred. Or to quote MLK for an example of what I am talking about<b></b>:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;First, I must confess that over the last few years I have been gravely disappointed with the white moderate. I have almost reached the regrettable conclusion that the Negro's great stumbling block in the stride toward freedom is not the White Citizen's Council-er or the Ku Klux Klanner, but the white moderate who is more devoted to &quot;order&quot; than to justice; who prefers a negative peace which is the absence of tension to a positive peace which is the presence of justice; who constantly says &quot;I agree with you in the goal you seek, but I can't agree with your methods of direct action;&quot; who paternalistically feels he can set the timetable for another man's freedom; who lives by the myth of time and who constantly advises the Negro to wait until a &quot;more convenient season.&quot;<br /> <br /> Shallow understanding from people of goodwill is more frustrating than absolute misunderstanding from people of ill will. Lukewarm acceptance is much more bewildering than outright rejection.&quot; </div> </div> </div>From Reverend Martin Luther King, Jr.'s <a href=\"http://www.hartford-hwp.com/archives/45a/060.html\" target=\"_blank\">Letter from Birmingham Jail.</a><br /> <br /> Or more to the point, the Syndicate has a lot of influence over the economy, but the wage gap (both gender and race) still exists, and gets worse the higher up you go in any given corporation. Just as one example. The Technocracy may ideally want to move past these attitudes, but the reality is that they're firmly entrenched in them. So are the Traditions in a lot of ways.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2367,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","user":"Resplendent Fire","date":". 10-23-2016, 08:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T19:10:37-07:00","id":992173,"title":"","content":"The reason bigotry survives in an organization that considers bigotry unscientific and absurd is multi-layered.<br /> (1)The guys at the top are often centuries old thanks to biological and cybernetic magitech. So their biases are very entrenched, even if they were politically liberal by the standards of their time.<br /> <br /> (2)The organization is secretive and top-down. This means that the more egregious acts of bigotry are often committed by men who are powerful, entrenched, and have institutions in place designed specifically to cover up whatever they are doing.<br /> <br /> (3)The very non-democratic nature of the organization means that successors are hand-picked by the older rulers, who in turn pick people they like. So even the younger rulers of the Technocracy have an old-boy mentality, having been hand-picked by the old-boys-club.<br /> <br /> The result is an organization that is deeply hypocritical. The guys up top are aware that many of the young science-nerds who make up their rank-n-file are often deeply liberal in every sense except perhaps loving order a bit more than freedom. So they pay lip-service to most liberal ideals. But they themselves often embody the worst aspects of old-boys-club establishment types, entitled and obsessed with keeping themselves on-top, rich, and privileged.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T19:16:03-07:00","id":992175,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3598_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3598\" data-vbnamecard=\"3598\">CajunKhan</a> Thank you. I was trying and failing to put that into words.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T19:23:31-07:00","id":992176,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/992033-so-i-finally-got-the-m20-core-book-my-complaints-aren-t-what-i-expected-them-to-be?p=992173#post992173\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The reason bigotry survives in an organization that considers bigotry unscientific and absurd is multi-layered.<br /> (1)The guys at the top are often centuries old thanks to biological and cybernetic magitech. So their biases are very entrenched, even if they were politically liberal by the standards of their time.<br /> <br /> (2)The organization is secretive and top-down. This means that the more egregious acts of bigotry are often committed by men who are powerful, entrenched, and have institutions in place designed specifically to cover up whatever they are doing.<br /> <br /> (3)The very non-democratic nature of the organization means that successors are hand-picked by the older rulers, who in turn pick people they like. So even the younger rulers of the Technocracy have an old-boy mentality, having been hand-picked by the old-boys-club.<br /> <br /> The result is an organization that is deeply hypocritical. The guys up top are aware that many of the young science-nerds who make up their rank-n-file are often deeply liberal in every sense except perhaps loving order a bit more than freedom. So they pay lip-service to most liberal ideals. But they themselves often embody the worst aspects of old-boys-club establishment types, entitled and obsessed with keeping themselves on-top, rich, and privileged.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except those &quot;Guys at the top&quot; are dead. Or rather disembodied. And one of them was a giant Spirit-AI who hated flesh in general. Hardly likely to be partisan to one gender over another.<br /> <br /> And yet the head of the NWO, and thus the union as a whole, is a woman.<br /> <br /> Except again, the current rulers of the Technocracy were selected after the unexpected and total destruction of their predecessors. The &quot;old boys club&quot; excuse thus holds no water.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T19:46:16-07:00","id":992186,"title":"","content":"Well then the Technocracy doesn't make any sense. They are written largely as a parody of The Establishment, and all the old-boys-networks that make it so corrupt, yet there are details to the organization that should make this impossible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T20:20:45-07:00","id":992203,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>C.S. Lewis</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u201cOf all tyrannies, a tyranny sincerely exercised for the good of its victims may be the most oppressive. It would be better to live under robber barons than under omnipotent moral busybodies. The robber baron's cruelty may sometimes sleep, his cupidity may at some point be satiated; but those who torment us for our own good will torment us without end for they do so with the approval of their own conscience.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>That has always been the defining feature of the Union to me. Good intentions justifying endless horrors. &quot;We're fighting for a better world! Why are you opposing that? If you oppose <b>that</b> you must be evil and WORTHY of destruction. Would you want the world to be <i>worse?!</i> How unmutual of you.&quot;<br /> <br /> On the other side of the coin you have the Traditions, who hide any number of nasty foibles. But at the same time, won't go out of their way to force those foibles upon you. For the most part anyway. They have a collective culture of &quot;Just build a fence and leave one another alone.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T23:57:57-07:00","id":992291,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/992033-so-i-finally-got-the-m20-core-book-my-complaints-aren-t-what-i-expected-them-to-be?p=992073#post992073\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What do the Disparates want aside from to punch those other two in the face? What binds them together? The Ali Bahtin are cited as one of the founding members but they only joined because the Technocracy is supposedly controlled by the Nephandi. According to who? According to, at the time the Children of Knowledge. Because the organization of subtle scholars who observe people for years just happen to be hanging out in &quot;the global club scene.&quot; alongside the LSD tripping rave cultists.</div> </div> </div> </div>Speaking of the LSD tripping rave cultists, I don't like how M20's section on the Children of Knowledge focuses heavily on that segment of its membership. It's not that I don't want players to run those kinds of characters. It's a valid interpretation of Alchemy. That's not my problem.<br /> <br /> It's that there are no old school alchemists. Where are the heirs to potion mixing scholars and metal purifying proto-chemists? Where are the seekers of immortality and transcendence? Dammit, where are the Fullmetal Alchemist clones, mixing arcane designs with militarism? How about Solificati who blend traditional methods with modern tools, like hallucinogenic smoke grenades, tattooed transmutation circles, and bullets propelled by alchemically perfected gunpowder?<br /> <br /> I don't want the Children of Knowledge - the Crowned Ones - to be reduced to nothing more than a cheap knockoff of the Cult of Ecstasy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T03:22:18-07:00","id":992314,"title":"","content":"What binds the Disparates together is, if you boil it down, indeed the desire to 'punch the two others in the face'.<br /> Essentially the problem of the Disparates is the power of not just the Technocracy, but also the Traditions.<br /> <br /> The Technocracy's power doesn't need explanation, and for the Disparates banding together is a matter of pure survival, where the Technocracy is concerned. They perfectly mirror the Traditions in that regard.<br /> Where the Traditions are concerned, the Disparates banded together on their own instead of joining them, for several reasons:<br /> <br /> 1) The founders of the new Disparates union were pissed at the Traditions.<br /> The Ahl-I-Batin because of the Traditions neglecting the middle east in the war against the Technocracy, which caused the Ahl-I-Batin to leave the Traditions in the first place.<br /> The Hollow Ones for how they have been repeatedly treated, neglected and ridiculed by the Traditions when they *were* making an effort to actually join them, for decades. This further discouraged other Disparates from joining; See below.<br /> <br /> For the other members of the Disparates the reasons vary a little, but it's a mixture of things:<br /> 2) Knowledge that joining the Traditions would merely make them some miniscule subgroups absorbed into some larger Tradition they don't identify with;<br /> 3) Lack of influence when it comes to not just their own Tradition, but the Council as a whole. Their voices would not be heard.<br /> 4) An overall disagreement with the very concept of the Ascension War. This is actually one of the stronger reasons why the Disparates did not just reject joining the Traditions, but actually plan on subtly work against them; They see the results of the Ascension War between Traditions and Technocracy as bad fallout for the sleeper landscape, as well as the metaphysical one. Not just in the way that Technocratic domination shaped the world into something more sterile and magick-rejecting, but also the hubris of both sides in both, claiming to know what's best for the world and the sleepers, and also the denial and neglecting of viewpoints, crafts and magick that does belong to anybody not a member of the Traditions. The way the Hollow Ones were treated served as the perfect example for that; And unlike some even more exotic crafts, the Hollow Ones were at least acknowledged as their own valid autonomous group.<br /> 5) The presumed Nephandic corruption, not only in the Technocracy but also the Traditions. In my opinion less of a reason to actually start the Disparates group, and more used as a reason to further underline the image of a common enemy in order to lessen friction between the Disparate parties.<br /> <br /> And thus, out of necessity of survival, as well as growing anger and rejection of the Status Quo, the Disparates joined together. It's stated in M20 that it's an uneasy union, as the Disparates *among themselves* have not much in common, but they have enough things that keep them wanting to work together. In that regard, they are just like the other two groups; A union out of practical, external reasons.<br /> <br /> Is the banding-together of the Disparates a smart move?<br /> Maybe they could have survived better against the Technocracy on their own, by staying in their own isolated, small groups. Maybe them commiting espionage and sabotage against not just the Technocracy but also the Traditions is the Worst Move Ever, should it come to light.<br /> And last but not least, how long can such a banding together that depends on utmost secrecy fly under the radar now?<br /> <br /> We'll see, I guess.<br /> <br /> <br /> Right now they don't matter in the grand scheme of things yet, but depending on how much they will have built up resources and power *when* (not if) their existance is revealed to the other groups, they might become an important established and disruptive third party in Mage politics as the Anarchs are in the Vampire landscape.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 10-24-2016, 06:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T08:57:30-07:00","id":992400,"title":"","content":"This is headcanon for me, but I imagine the Disparates to be primarily architected by the Ahl-i-Batin. Remember that their ideal is Unity; it makes sense that if they decided the Traditions weren't up to the job of unifying humanity, they'd find some other group to help them with it. That's what they <i>do</i>. I like the idea of a Batini stepping out of shadows at a bunch of isolated, ragged Crafts: &quot;Technocracy got you down? Traditions not helping? Come hang with <i>my</i> friends...&quot;<br /> <br /> There are a lot of reasons to dislike the Disparates in the metaplot (technephandi among them), so I won't belabor that point. One of the things I <i>do</i> like is that they give us a chance to rejuvenate Crafts of which our most recent mention had been, &quot;I think they all got killed by HIT Marks.&quot; The Taftani is a good example - sure you have some old masters holding out in Iran after the revolution, nurturing a little reality zone, but they're still threatened by technology; what happens when the Iranian government wants to put a new set of centrifuges under that mountain you bound your djinni into? So you also have a bunch of young guns in Dubai, showing that <i>Asha</i> and technology are compatible. It's very appealing to extend the implausible real-world Dubai into an actually-impossible WoD one, with architecture that defies gravity and rich new lands raised from the drowning ocean.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7356-haldir2012","name":"haldir2012","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T11:19:56-07:00","id":992495,"title":"","content":"I think that a lot of the bad press that the Disparates get comes from the necessary editing that happened to keep the size of M20 within printable bounds. Each of them require almost and entire Tradition book, or at least a writeup comparable to their chapters in Lost Paths and The Book of Crafts, to fully get across their individual nuance. I think that their basic writeups that made it through to M20 was a cut down distillation to what the author might have thought the easiest take-aways. <br /> <br /> The Children of Knowledge certainly suffer from this, with their deep ties with LSD, but they never fully escaped it in their original writeup either. It's in fact the catalyst of their reappearance in modern times. It's easy to get caught up in the comparison to the Cult of Ecstasy, but the distinction lies in the philosophy of each. The Ecstatics may use substances to induce altered mind-states, it's for the purpose of perspective and sensation, to experience reality differently so as to alter it. On the other hand, the Children, those that do use LSD for their magicks, do so to fundamentally alter themselves, to purify and reforge. It might look the same at the start, but taking their beliefs contribute to a very different culture, and IIRC this is at least somewhat evident in their M20 writeup.<br /> <br /> The Taftani are certainly the most altered from their original presentation, but it was probably done for the sake of a more cohesive theme in the book, that Paradox is bad and we try not to fuck with it. While the Taftani's flagrant rebellion against the Technocratic Consensus was pretty vital to their philosophy, it's dissonant from the rest of the book and might confuse unfamiliar players, especially those who are already chaffing at the idea of such a restrictive system. Instead, their writeup focused on their domination of djinni and application of art and craft into their magicks, which is probably more helpful.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, Mage is such a huge game that the attempt at including everything in one book ended up doing disservice to many of the more interesting elements.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6384-frozenfishy","name":"Frozenfishy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6384_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T11:27:18-07:00","id":992505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/992033-so-i-finally-got-the-m20-core-book-my-complaints-aren-t-what-i-expected-them-to-be#post992033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Secondly, And I feel this is largely connected to the first. The one size fits all Paradigm descriptions, while they speed play and character creation, distract from the internal philosophy of each faction and reduce them to interchangeable buzzwords. THIS is why the Disparate alliance felt so.... empty. Because all the intricate beliefs about how and why they do what they do were replaced with politics. Everything was about how the other two factions screwed them over and so they needed to make a third.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Paradigms as presented in M20 are the core of an individual's beliefs, not the entirety of it. The beliefs of the group flavor the personal Paradigm. How a SoE views 'A Mechanistic Cosmos' is different from his It-X counterpart to say nothing of a OoH member viewing that Paradigm. M20 Paradigms are common Paradigms stripped down to the base level, a skeleton of a mage's beliefs. It's the fleshing out of the character that adds the muscle and skin to the skeleton.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}